ll pretty nice there you get into the  biggest airtime Hill to ride which is  already a lot more violent than anything  so far in the ride and then you go into  these twisted airtime Hills which is  personally my favorite part because  these really throw you out of your seat  pretty violently and the ride ends with  a bunch of small bunny hops with again  some pretty good airtime before you go  back into the station so all-in-all this  layout might just be the most  perfect layout for its size I honestly  cannot imagine making a better layout  for how small this ride is you get a  really wide range of airtime some nice  spacing and super smooth curves all I  can say is that there should definitely  be more of these intimate mega lights in  the world  [Music]  so tobe zoo isn't only about cover semi  there's also Regina which is by far the  second best ride in the park I would say  and arguably the best wooden roller  coaster in Japan considering how few  there are in Japan it's not that much of  an achievement but if you're a fan of  classic Woody's then this is probably  the best thing you'll get it's also a  rare coaster with a distinctly female  name and logo and everything even the  advertisement for it back in the day  managed to sexually objectify a roller  coaster of all things but I guess we can  chalk that up to Japan being Japan  anyway it's a fun ride and it's a really  nice bonus when you go there to ride  cover semi I wouldn't say that it's  something to travel to the park for and  go out of your way to ride but it's just  a really classic out in back layouts  with some drops and mostly on banked  turns there's not a lot of airtime on it  and it's pretty shaky but it's not  shakey to the point where it's  uncomfortable I think it just  contributes to the the out of control  wooden coaster fuel that you get on the  ride so overall great wooden coaster  probably the best in Japan and  definitely pick it up if you're at the  park anyway  [Music]  now this 